WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.720
I'm selling all the retro gaming stuff from the 80s,

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.680
Most of them are Gameboys,

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.160
PC Engine,

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:29.960
SNK Neo Geo Systems

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.440
SEGA, and many others.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.040
Before I started this shop, I was in the video game business

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:39.560
That was way back in the 90s if I'm not wrong

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:43.800
I got very serious into this gaming business,

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:44.840
and that's where I am now.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:52.120
All the retro stuff I have now, are from my personal collection through the years.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:56.080
I'm interested in retro gaming collection,

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:59.760
In terms of playing, I'm not a true gamer

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.000
I don't really play games that well.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:06.000
I started collecting because I liked the items,

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.600
When I find that they are funny or cute,

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:12.080
or if they intricate me, I will put them aside.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:17.080
Most of what I have today, that is how I collected them.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:18.400
Because at that point of time, 

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:24.200
I would not have known that people will collect retro gaming stuff.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:29.320
For myself I like playing with Gameboys

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:31.720
Like the very first Gameboy Classic, 

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:34.040
The grey one that came with Tetris

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:36.440
That is still my favourite game.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:38.560
For me this is the easiest game to play

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:39.960
for young and old,

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:46.680
until today, I think some of the older folks are still looking around for this game.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:52.040
The first game that I ever bought was with my own pocket money

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:54.600
At that time, it was around $28

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:58.200
It was a Nintendo Game &amp; Watch, Manhole

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:03.080
Those Game &amp; Watch in the shop now are for sale but,

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:11.520
a lot of customers are looking for one because it makes them think back on their childhood.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:16.200
Some of the Game &amp; Watch sets are worth a lot of money now

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:19.560
From as low as $80-90 to

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:23.600
brand new, sealed in box at a few thousand dollars.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:28.760
Retro gaming is like collecting antiques

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:31.680
At that time, the most expensive system

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:34.960
was the SNK Neo Geo

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:39.720
Some of the brand new games cost up to about S$800.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:45.280
When I started to sell it, it was considered a rich man's game machine.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:49.840
The one piece that is worth a lot in the retro gaming market now,

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:57.960
is the Metal Slug, USA Version

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:03.480
My dream is actually to open a retro gaming museum

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.480
but it seems like I can't fulfill that dream

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:15.480
Due to circumstances such as difficulty in finding a space

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:20.560
So instead of letting keeping all this

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:24.600
I might as well sell them to real collectors

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:30.960
For casual gamers, they would think its a waste of money  

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:32.960
But for those who are into retro gaming,  

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:37.680
when they see this collection,

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:41.120
they might get quite envious.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:46.400
My wife for one, says that it is a waste of money and space

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:51.960
till the day she realised that some of the items are worth so much.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:04:00.120
Most of the retro gaming machines I have now are in good working condition. 

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:04.360
The technology at that time is very different from now.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:06.560
Those games are burned into EEPROM

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:09.680
Until today they are still working because there are less moving parts

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.640
I think it will last for many years to come.

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:15.160
Seriously, new gaming sucks.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:18.120
this is part of the reason why people go back to playing retro games.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:24.680
for example, Super Shinobi Shadow Dancer, beats any of the PS4 games, hands down.

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:28.920
Graphics are fantastic

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:32.680
They spend a lot of time and effort to create beautiful graphics

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:35.560
but, no gameplay and replay value.

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:37.960
Spend $80, 6 hours complete. 

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:41.120
During my overseas trips,

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:43.440
I like to visit gaming shops

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:47.400
So I saw retro gaming in Japan

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.960
but in Singapore, there is none

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:52.720
So I thought, why not start a shop in Singapore?

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:54.400
I'm proud to be the first,

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:58.520
but I'm not sure how it would go from here on out.

